      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "Unit tests covered the navigator.share, clipboard and error branches but could not prove the toast actually rendered end to end; the e2e specs drive the branches through the existing window.__PLAYWRIGHT__ analytics seam rather than stubbing fetch."
    },
    {
      "id": "docs_superpowers_plans_archive_2026_05_13_verify_animations_and_share_animation_interrupt_coverage",
      "label": "Animation interrupt coverage (4 cases)",
      "file_type": "rationale",
      "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/archive/2026-05-13-verify-animations-and-share.md",
      "source_location": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "Rapid Continue, Escape mid-reveal, Escape mid-panel-slide-in and hash mutation mid-animation had no coverage. The tests key on data-animation-state=\"entering\" instead of wall-clock timing, so they assert the interrupt happens genuinely mid-animation without sleeping."
    },
    {
      "id": "docs_superpowers_plans_archive_2026_05_13_verify_animations_and_share_mcp_visual_verification",
      "label": "Playwright MCP state-signaled visual verification",
      "file_type": "rationale",
      "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/archive/2026-05-13-verify-animations-and-share.md",
      "source_location": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "Visual polish cannot be asserted by a test, so screenshots are captured at state-signaled frames and reconciled against the documented unhappy-path scenarios, with a scope guardrail limiting in-line fixes to trivial deviations."
    },
    {
      "id": "docs_superpowers_plans_archive_2026_05_13_verify_animations_and_share_coverage_gap_rating",
      "label": "Coverage gaps that held ratings below 9",
